            <ArticleTitle>[Robert's uterus with menstrual retention in the blind cavity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>366-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Robert's uterus or asymmetric septate uterus is a rare malformation. It presents with two cavities, one of which is blind. The authors report an original case: the blind cavity, on the right side of the septum, contained retained secretions. The embryologic and physiopathologic mechanism of this anomaly still are to be discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
